# Step 2 — OSS Remediation — P1 only

Use APP_NAME, HIGHLIGHT_NAME, and HIGHLIGHT_APP_ID already resolved in this conversation.
Do not ask the user to re-enter them.
If any are missing from context, say so and stop — do not guess.

Input: #file:oss_remediation_plan.md

## Pre-flight checks
1. `get_application_info` name=HIGHLIGHT_NAME → must return results.
2. Confirm `oss_remediation_plan.md` exists in the workspace and contains a P1 section.
If either fails: stop and report to user — do not proceed.

## Rules (one P1 item at a time)

1. Work P1 items in order: P1.1, P1.2, … one at a time.

2. Before each fix, run the full workspace dependency analysis:
   Follow #file:.github/skills/workspace-dependency-analysis.md exactly.
   Inputs: component name and detected version from oss_remediation_plan.md.
   Wait for the blast radius report before proceeding.

2b. Cross-validate manifest files:
   pom.xml · package.json · requirements.txt · build.gradle · *.csproj
   Workspace source code is ground truth — if declared version differs from Highlight, note discrepancy.
   Never skip if workspace search returns no results — the component may be a transitive dependency.

3. Apply the decision gate from the skill:
   - Blocker present → stop, present blast radius report to user, await explicit confirmation.
   - No blocker → proceed to fix.
   - Usage not locatable → skip fix, flag for manual investigation, move to next P1 item.

4. Apply fix using nearest safe version from oss_remediation_plan.md.
   Use latest safe only if nearest safe breaks a confirmed dependency.

5. Wrap all modified lines:
   ```
   // AI remediation begin — <component> <old_version> → <new_version>
   <changed lines>
   // AI remediation end
   ```

6. Run build after each fix:
   - Pass → move to next action.
   - Fail → revert, log failure with reason, skip to next action.

7. After all P1 items, output completion summary:
   | Item | Component | Old Ver | New Ver | Result | Notes |
   |------|-----------|---------|---------|--------|-------|

## Do not
- Re-ask for any app name or IDs already in conversation context.
- Fix P2 or P3 items in this session.
- Batch multiple component changes.
- Proceed past a build failure without reverting.
- Treat workspace silence as confirmation a component is unused — it may be a transitive dependency.

## Start
Complete pre-flight checks, then begin P1.1 from oss_remediation_plan.md.
